The mapping behavior appears unchanged, but the new diagnostic can conflate per-benchmark AIG IDs and report unrelated selected matches. This undermines the accuracy of the feature introduced by the patch.

Review comment:

- [P2] Scope watched AIG IDs per source benchmark — /Users/cunxiy/Documents/research/autoresearch-eda/abc-harness/src/map/mapper/mapperMatch.c:1436-1436
  When `stmap75` is run across the benchmark suite, this single watch list is applied to every network even though mapper AIG IDs are only meaningful within one input design. IDs that came from another benchmark can therefore match unrelated nodes and be counted/printed as final-critical selected matches, making the new selected-match stats false positives; pass or filter benchmark/network-specific watch IDs before logging.
